{"shortDescription":"Central European currencies were weaker on Monday as the dollar firmed ahead of a Federal Reserve interest-rate decision and a rise in oil prices dampened risk sentiment.","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Central European currencies were weaker on Monday as the dollar firmed ahead of a Federal Reserve interest-rate decision and a rise in oil prices dampened risk sentiment."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Investors will also be watching a series of data from the region, with current account data from Poland and the Czech Republic on Monday, as well as Polish CPI, core inflation and industrial output later in the week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["PKO BP economists said local data could influence the zloty, but the external environment — including energy commodity price trends — should continue to exert the dominant influence on the currency."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The week's key event will be Wednesday's (Fed) decision; given current market sentiment, a decision not to raise Fed rates could trigger a moderate depreciation of the dollar,\" they said in a note."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"Nevertheless, we assess the risk balance as unfavourable for the zloty; consequently, we anticipate the EUR/PLN exchange rate rising to the 4.33–4.34 range and USD/PLN moving towards 3.74–3.75 over the course of the week.\""]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The zloty (EURPLN) was 0.2% weaker at 4.3315 per euro at 0755 GMT."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The main event of the week in the region will be Thursday's Czech National Bank interest-rate decision."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The outcome of the CNB meeting will be a key focus this week; we anticipate that the central bank can comfortably maintain rates at 3.75% for the time being,\" Bank CSOB said in a note."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"However, rising energy prices could gradually alter the landscape, making a further rate hike highly plausible at the November meeting.\""]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The crown ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURCZK","text":"OANDA:EURCZK"}}," was 0.1% lower at 24.2850 per euro, while the Hungarian forint ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX:EURHUF","text":"FX:EURHUF"}}," weakened by 0.45% to 365.00. Hungary's central bank (MNB) holds its next rate-setting meeting on September 22."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"Between June and August, the MNB delivered a total of 75 basis points of rate cuts, bringing the policy rate down from 6.25% to 5.50%. We maintain our year-end policy rate forecast of 5%, although upside risks to the interest-rate trajectory have increased,\" Erste Group said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"As geopolitical tensions have intensified again, developments in energy prices, particularly natural gas prices, remain the key determinant of the forint's performance.\""]}]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":3},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT  0955 CET"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CURRENCIES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latest trade"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Previous close"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"